Here's how to implement all three requirements:

### 1 & 2. Intercept Back Navigation with a Confirmation Dialog

Override `OnBackButtonPressed` in your page:

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (!_hasUnsavedChanges)
            return base.OnBackButtonPressed();

        // Fire-and-forget since the override is synchronous
        Dispatcher.Dispatch(async () =>
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (leave)
                await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
        });

        return true; // cancel the default navigation
    }
}
```

> **Key point:** `OnBackButtonPressed` returns `bool` (not `Task`), so you dispatch the async dialog work separately and return `true` immediately to block the default navigation.

### 3. Custom "Cancel" Back Button

Replace Shell's default back button via the toolbar:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
             Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{StaticResource CancelBackButton}">

    <Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
        <BackButtonBehavior Command="{Binding CancelCommand}"
                            TextOverride="Cancel"
                            IconOverride="" />
    </Shell.BackButtonBehavior>

    <!-- page content -->
</ContentPage>
```

Wire up the command in your view model (or code-behind):

```csharp
public ICommand CancelCommand { get; }

public EditProductPage()
{
    InitializeComponent();

    CancelCommand = new Command(async () =>
    {
        if (!_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
            return;
        }

        bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
            "Unsaved Changes",
            "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
            "Discard", "Stay");

        if (leave)
            await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    });

    BindingContext = this;
}
```

### How the pieces fit together

| Scenario | Handled by |
|---|---|
| Android hardware/gesture back | `OnBackButtonPressed` override |
| Shell toolbar back button | `BackButtonBehavior.Command` |
| Swipe-back (iOS) | `BackButtonBehavior` disables it when a command is set |

Set `_hasUnsavedChanges = true` whenever form fields change (e.g., via `TextChanged` events or property setters in your view model).
